  "title": "Quantum mechanics is the singular limit of a finite theory",
  "statements": [
    {
      "id": "69e174a7-c135-4862-aaf4-686db8dfe43e",
      "text": "The state space of quantum mechanics is a singular limit, at $p = \\infty$, of a discretized Hilbert space, and does not arise smoothly as $p \\rightarrow \\infty$. The Schrödinger and Dirac equations describe evolution on $I_U$ in that limit.",
